Goal: close the missing Phase 18 header inventory and reverse-frame evidence for
the already implemented `GetTopicsByClusterRequestHeader`, on branch
`phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`.

Changes:
- Added `GetTopicsByClusterRequestHeader` to the Protocol header inventory and
  validation matrix. Its Java constructor, getter, setter, and no-op
  `checkFields` API inventory is recorded in the query-admin decode fixture.
- Added the request-224 typed Rust frame with `cluster=cluster-a` to the
  Java cross-decode generator and verifier, raising the exact header count
  from 67 to 68.
- Replaced randomized `Map.of`-derived `KVTable` fixture order with explicit
  insertion order. `fixtures/producer/core.json` SHA-256:
  `861cc12c939270c338349d9ec343a4aaceb8e987031c99c016f75e03df4537c1`.
- Updated request-code and Java compatibility evidence and the release
  checklist. The pinned Phase 18 plan was not edited.

Verification passed:
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --locked --test headers
  header_validation_matrix`
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --locked --test header_inventory`
- `cargo test --workspace --locked`
- `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked`
- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D
  warnings`
- `mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify` (37 invoked RPC scenarios,
  68 Rust typed-header frames, 15 typed-body fixtures, and Java/Rust
  cross-decodes)
- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and `git diff --check`

This closes only the named header inventory and reverse-frame evidence gap.
Broad P18-V01 and P18-V02/P18-V03/P18-V04 remain open. The four Phase 19
working-tree paths were left untouched and unstaged.
